Three systems diagrams in papers/architecture/paper.md adapt Will Cook's
"A Repository-Based System for Research and Publication" in wcook04/plectis-erdos,
revision 61fb590921e3b5a100dc264bed052c9cf6959daf, under CC-BY-4.0.
Their content has been redrawn for this repository's workflow and evidence
boundaries. The current figures identify shared passages, joint mathematical
inputs, and two authored expansion links with a citation-to-source route.
Exact source, figure identifiers, relation meanings and licence links are
recorded in papers/architecture/README.md.

An earlier edition's opening funnel adapted Will Cook's mathematics-map film
composition for its reader groups and source-navigation paths. It did not
reproduce the film's result-specific examples, page counts or verification
claims. The current companion replaces that funnel with three accounts mapped
to shared support.

The gap-area figure in papers/qaoa-sk/expository/main.md adapts the
gap-convexity figure from OpenAI's "Full support of the zero-temperature
Sherrington-Kirkpatrick order parameter," in OpenAI/math revision
adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a, under Apache-2.0.
The adaptation relabels the endpoints, uses grayscale shading and explains
the schematic area comparison. The original source and licence remain in
examples/qaoa-sk/upstream/; the figure caption identifies the source.

